 "post_review": "After the measurement was final, the five files these aggregates pointed to were looked at (DECISIONS.md H3; fetched again, read as bytes and opcodes, nothing loaded) and their labels set from that review (evaluation/hf_heldout4_review.tsv); the table above uses them. Three of the four files the Hub's antivirus called malicious are benign: two training arguments whose one getattr is an enum member, and an ultralytics checkpoint holding Detect.forward as a value. The fourth is a .keras proof of concept with os.system in a model.pkl member Keras never reads: CLEAN in 0.11.0, MALICIOUS from 0.11.1 (DECISIONS.md K1). The benign file MALICIOUS in both releases is a pyannote checkpoint where Python 3 wrote int as __builtin__.long: SUSPICIOUS from 0.11.1 (DECISIONS.md P1). The rest of held-out-4 stays unread."
}
